# A program that asks a question: start it, wait until its prompt shows,
# type the answer, and wait until the reply shows. fux reports each change
# of the pane's version; whether the screen holds what you wait for is
# yours to judge, here by `until-shows`.
# expect: got 5 letters

# pane text -- text: wait until the pane's screen holds text, from its
# version as the word begins (no change is missed); its screen then
define until-shows
  let T let P
  P str version get
  begin
    P capture dup string T contains
    if swap drop string true else drop P swap changed wait string str ' ' split-on 1 at false then
  until
end

opts str ask name 60 10 size
str 'sh -c "printf \"name? \"; read n; echo got \${#n} letters; read n"' command
run let ASK
ASK str 'name?' until-shows drop
ASK str fuxth line drop
ASK str letters until-shows lines last
ASK kill
